From f4e33bac62ce69d65a76384d9cba557d80af3258 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CBS Radio Platform <dev@ephraitech.example>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:04:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] fix: correct the defects found while writing the
 PHPUnit suite

Each of these was found by a test written for the behaviour it should have had. Against the code before this
commit 56 of the 894 tests fail; after it, all pass.

- Editing a category or vendor without renaming it saved nothing and showed no error (the {id} placeholder of the
  is_unique rule was never filled by update()).
- A booking that failed to save kept its place on the show, and one failed query left every later transaction on
  the connection failing (strict transaction mode keeps the status false).
- A hand-made request could store a negative package or gift price, impossible show days, or crash the show form.
- find(null) means "every row": a booking with no category, a gift order with no gift, or a vendor gift with no
  vendor was treated as matching all of them.
- FileManager served and deleted any path, including ../ climbs and the session and log folders.
- A category switched off was still bookable by its address; the booking date accepted "next friday".
- The ffprobe availability check was cached once per process rather than per path; the "already processed" guard in
  the voice-note validator could never run.
- Lists sorted only by a one-second timestamp could reshuffle same-second rows.

GiftOrderService and GiftVendorSyncService gain an overridable vendorClient() so a test can supply a fake vendor
instead of reaching a real one.
